  "title": "Vertically opposite angles, straight lines and angles at a point",
  "summary": "Apply the three core angle facts at intersections and around a point.",
  "outcomes": [
    "1.2"
  ],
  "prerequisite_lessons": [
    "g1-lesson-01"
  ],
  "estimated_minutes": 55,
  "objectives": [
    "Apply vertically opposite, straight-line and angles-at-a-point facts.",
    "Form equations from angle expressions at intersections.",
    "Check that calculated angles satisfy the relevant 180° or 360° total."
  ],
  "mastery_policy_key": "g1-default-v1",
  "sections": [
    {
      "stable_key": "g1-12-method",
      "position": 1,
      "type": "explanation",
      "title": "Three local angle facts",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Vertically opposite angles are equal, adjacent angles on a straight line total 180°, and angles around a point total 360°."
        },
        {
          "type": "display_math",
          "latex": "\\text{opposite: equal}\\qquad\\text{line: }180^\\circ\\qquad\\text{point: }360^\\circ"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stable_key": "g1-lesson-02-visual",
      "position": 2,
      "type": "explanation",
      "title": "Read the diagram",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The diagram shows two straight lines crossing, with each obtuse angle marked 124° and the acute angles marked a and b. Vertically opposite angles are the pair across the vertex from each other, and they are equal. Adjacent angles on a straight line total 180°, and all four angles around the point total 360°."
        },
        {
          "type": "asset_ref",
          "asset_key": "g1-lesson-02-diagram"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stable_key": "g1-lesson-02-reasoning",
      "position": 3,
      "type": "explanation",
      "title": "Reasoning method",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When algebraic expressions label vertically opposite angles, equate them. When expressions label an adjacent linear pair, add them and set the sum to 180°. A reliable check is to alternate the two angle sizes around a two-line intersection and verify that all four total 360°."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stable_key": "g1-12-example",
      "position": 4,
      "type": "worked_example",
      "title": "Worked example: angles at an intersection",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In the diagram, two straight lines cross and each obtuse angle is 124°. Find the acute angles a and b."
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "position": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Angle a and a 124° angle are adjacent on a straight line, so they total 180°."
            },
            {
              "type": "display_math",
              "latex": "a=180^\\circ-124^\\circ=56^\\circ"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 2,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Angle b is vertically opposite angle a, so they are equal."
            },
            {
              "type": "display_math",
              "latex": "b=56^\\circ"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "verification_note": "Going round the point: 124° + 56° + 124° + 56° = 360°."
    },
    {
      "stable_key": "g1-lesson-02-example-2",
      "position": 5,
      "type": "worked_example",
      "title": "Worked example: vertically opposite expressions",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Vertically opposite angles are (5x + 7)° and (8x − 38)°. Find every angle at the intersection."
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "position": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Vertically opposite angles are equal."
            },
            {
              "type": "display_math",
              "latex": "5x+7=8x-38"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 2,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "display_math",
              "latex": "45=3x\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x=15"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Each angle of that pair is 5(15) + 7 = 82°."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Each adjacent angle is 180° − 82° = 98°, so the four angles are 82°, 98°, 82° and 98°."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "verification_note": "Both expressions give 82° when x = 15, and 82 + 98 + 82 + 98 = 360."
    },
    {
      "stable_key": "g1-lesson-02-pitfalls",
      "position": 6,
      "type": "explanation",
      "title": "Common errors and checks",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Do not equate adjacent angles unless another fact says they are equal. A straight line gives a total of 180°, while angles around a point give 360°. State the angle fact before writing the equation so the correct total is clear."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stable_key": "g1-12-recall",
      "position": 7,
      "type": "active_recall",
      "title": "Check your understanding",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "One angle on a straight line is 73°. Find the other."
        }
      ],
      "response": {
        "type": "numeric",
        "comparison_mode": "exact_numeric",
        "canonical_answer": "107",
        "canonical_latex": "107",
        "accepted_answers": [],
        "absolute_tolerance": null,
        "rounding_precision": null,
        "unit": null
      },
      "feedback": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Angles on a straight line total 180°, so 180 - 73 = 107."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stable_key": "g1-lesson-02-summary",
      "position": 8,
      "type": "summary",
      "title": "Method checklist",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Vertically opposite angles are equal; angles on a straight line total 180°; angles around a point total 360°."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Name the fact before writing the equation, and check that the four angles at a crossing total 360°."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
